Four <chloride ligands> give Ti(IV), $d^0$. Ionic <electron counting> gives
$$\boxed{N_e=0+4(2)=8.}$$
**<tetrahedral molecular geometry>** separates the four donors without placing them at $90^\circ$. A $d^0$ centre has no occupied <d orbitals> providing a square-planar stabilization; the 18-electron rule is not a requirement for this early-metal compound.

